{"title":"Square (geometry)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>square</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral\" title=\"Quadrilateral\">quadrilateral</a> in which all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">sides</a> have equal length and all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\"> angles</a> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle\" title=\"Right angle\">right angles</a>.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b099e8fd521b2fcda4322d23b57eb040ea4a5bf4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import markers; pair A, B, C, D;  A = (-1, 1); B = (1, 1); C = (1, -1); D = (-1, -1);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(rightanglemark(A, B, C)); draw(rightanglemark(B, C, D)); draw(rightanglemark(C, D, A)); draw(rightanglemark(D, A, B)); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, StickIntervalMarker(4)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Equivalently, all squares are the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polygon\" title=\"Regular polygon\">regular</a> quadrilaterals.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Area\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Area</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Perimeter\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Perimeter</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Diagonal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagonal</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Area\">Area</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Area\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a square can be found by squaring the square's side length: the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of a square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064e3f0bbcbe63f6670b54027df19eaaed0d7e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = s^2$\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Perimeter\">Perimeter</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Perimeter\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of a square can be found by multiplying the square's side length by four - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e55e2072e6922925ad3efcf0d80d44a2325ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 4s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagonal\">Diagonal</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Diagonal\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The length of either <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">diagonal</a> of a square can be obtained by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\"> Pythagorean theorem</a>. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97404df4a679d97c2ecc5da665c0b1ee2c7cc30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\sqrt{s^2+s^2}=s\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>You can also find the area of a square using its diagonal. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f48302525ed9df84c35e6770b068400b0f7d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${D^2}/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"21\" /> is equivalent to the area of a square.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Unit_Square\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Unit Square\">Unit Square</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube_(geometry)\" title=\"Cube (geometry)\"> Cube</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003605\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 70/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1656/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.597      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.597      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1844:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003605 and revision id 254924. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}